diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index c8a070b2a..6617c8add 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ Version 1.8.0 (2026-10-06)
 
 Enhancements
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
+- Generate dataset summary rows and tables dynamically from class ``METADATA`` (:class:`~moabb.datasets.metadata.schema.DatasetMetadata` + constructor attributes) and BIDS events/sidecars (``*_events.tsv``, ``*_channels.tsv``, ``*_eeg.json``, ``participants.tsv``) via :func:`~moabb.datasets.base.summary_row_from_metadata`, :func:`~moabb.datasets.base.summary_row_from_bids`, :func:`~moabb.datasets.base.build_summary_row`, :func:`~moabb.datasets.base.generate_summary_table`, and ``get_summary_table(..., from_metadata=True)``. :class:`~moabb.datasets.base.MetaclassDataset` now synthesizes ``_summary_table`` and the ``Dataset summary`` docstring admonition from ``METADATA`` when a dataset is not listed in ``summary_*.csv``, and :class:`~moabb.datasets.base.LocalBIDSDataset` populates ``_summary_table`` from its BIDS root (:gh:`1355`, :gh:`1356` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Speed up package imports, ``dataset_list`` construction, ``DATASET_METADATA_CATALOG`` lookups, dataset preprocessing, paradigms, evaluations, splitters, pipelines, and analysis/plotting across the library: PEP 562 ``__getattr__`` lazy loading across :mod:`moabb`, :mod:`moabb.datasets`, :mod:`moabb.paradigms`, :mod:`moabb.evaluations`, :mod:`moabb.pipelines`, and :mod:`moabb.analysis`; per-dataset lazy resolution in ``DATASET_METADATA_CATALOG``; cached ``mne.Info`` and contiguous array construction in :class:`~moabb.datasets.fake.FakeDataset` and :func:`~moabb.datasets.utils.build_raw_from_epochs`; fast-path stimulus channel discovery and vectorized sliding-window event generation in :mod:`moabb.datasets.preprocessing`; cached BIDS root/descriptor properties and fast cache-miss checks in :mod:`moabb.datasets.bids_interface`; shared-``Raw`` multi-band filtering and ``np.repeat`` metadata assembly in :meth:`moabb.paradigms.base.BaseProcessing.get_data`; direct trialwise leave-one-out scoring, precomputed metadata routing, vectorized splitter group indexing, and fast fold aggregation in :mod:`moabb.evaluations`; cached Chebyshev filter-bank design, vectorized 3D ``sosfiltfilt`` filtering, shared-QR CCA/itCCA/MsetCCA/eCCA scoring, vectorized TRCA/TRCA-R/SSCOR/TDCA covariance and shrinkage estimation, and faster :class:`~moabb.pipelines.csp.TRCSP` and :class:`~moabb.pipelines.features.StandardScaler_Epoch` in :mod:`moabb.pipelines`; and vectorized permutation/Wilcoxon/effect-size meta-analysis, cached pipeline digests, batched HDF5 reads/writes in :class:`~moabb.analysis.results.Results`, and precomputed ``@verbose`` argument binding in :mod:`moabb.utils` (:gh:`1153`, :gh:`1345`, :gh:`1351`, :gh:`1352` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Update :class:`moabb.datasets.Kueper2024` to version 2 of the release (Zenodo 17940098): six more subjects (9-14) from a second study, unilateral movements only; the EEG files of subjects 1-8 are unchanged. Add a ``rest`` class placed 3 s before each correct movement onset whose preceding rest lasted at least 5 s, so all 14 subjects can be evaluated with ``unilateral`` versus ``rest``. The second study has no motion-tracking marker, so its movement onset is the release of the right hand switch, which follows the motion-tracking onset by a median of 54 ms in the first study. Mark the dataset as movement execution (``detected_paradigm="motor_execution"``) and describe the trial protocol as the authors do: a rest of at least 5 s, the movement onset at 0 s, then self-paced execution (:gh:`1333` reported by `Niklas Kueper`_, fixed by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Add the tutorial :ref:`sphx_glr_auto_examples_how_to_benchmark_plot_cross_system_transfer_maskedmean.py`: cross-system transfer with a minimum distance to masked Riemannian mean, on datasets recorded with different montages and sampling rates, pooled in a :class:`~moabb.datasets.compound_dataset.CompoundDataset` and evaluated with :class:`~moabb.evaluations.CrossSubjectEvaluation` (``cv_class=LeaveOneGroupOut, groups="device"``). To support it, the evaluations route any metadata column of the training trials (``device``, ``dataset``, ``subject``...) to the pipeline steps that request it with scikit-learn metadata routing (``set_fit_request(device=True)``), and :class:`~moabb.datasets.fake.FakeDataset` takes a ``device`` (:gh:`1305` by `Quentin Barthelemy`_).
@@ -98,6 +99,7 @@ Requirements
 
 Bugs
 ~~~~
+- Second-pass paper-by-paper audit across all 206 dataset classes against their primary publications and repository records: fix channel-type mappings in :class:`moabb.datasets.BNCI2003_004` (``AA``..``AG`` set as ``eeg``, ``AH`` as ``eog``), :class:`moabb.datasets.Cattan2019_VR` (``Fp1`` kept as ``eeg``), :class:`moabb.datasets.Liu2024` (``ECG`` channel type ``ecg`` instead of ``misc``), and :class:`moabb.datasets.Huebner2017` / :class:`moabb.datasets.Huebner2018` (EOG channels ``EOGvu``/``EOGh``/``VEOG``/``HEOG`` counted in ``METADATA.acquisition.channel_types`` and ``AuxiliaryChannelsMetadata``), and enrich missing ``METADATA`` fields (demographics, hardware, references, filters, trial counts, DOIs, funding, ethics, and data URLs) across 137 dataset modules (:gh:`1350`, :gh:`1353` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Render motor-execution datasets (:class:`moabb.datasets.Thapa2025`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Kueper2024`, :class:`moabb.datasets.NeBULA2025`, :class:`moabb.datasets.PerezBlanco2026`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Schirrmeister2017`, :class:`moabb.datasets.GuttmannFlury2025_ME`, and :class:`moabb.datasets.Wu2020`) as **Motor Execution** instead of **Motor Imagery** in the automated Stimulus Protocol timeline diagram, dataset webpage header, and metadata catalog (reported by Bhoj Raj Thapa, fixed by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Kueper2024` keeping error trials (rest shorter than 5 s, marker ``S3``) and additional trials (``S27``) as movement events: only onsets followed by the end-of-correct-trial marker ``S128`` are kept, 40 per recording set. Also download the subjects a partial cache lacks instead of returning no runs: ``data_path`` checked only that the dataset folder existed, so a cache from version 1 or from the NEMAR deposit (subjects 1-8) would have loaded subjects 9-14 empty (:gh:`1333` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Cho2017` giving the pre-cue segment a class-dependent offset. The GigaDB files store each class as a stream of tiled 7-s trial blocks (2 s fixation, then the cue), and the loader removed the mean of each class stream as a whole; since some participants make a sustained eye movement toward the imagined hand after the cue, that mean differs by class, so without a high-pass filter (``fmin=None``) the pre-cue segment of every trial carried an offset of about half the post-cue step, with the opposite sign. The loader now removes from each block the mean of its own fixation period (subject 5, F8-F7 in the second before the cue, right minus left: -4313 before, +7 after, in file units). The default 8-32 Hz band and the default 0-3 s interval give identical data. A high-pass of 0.1-1 Hz removes the mean of the tiled block pattern itself and puts the offset back whatever the loader does; the docstring now documents the data layout and recommends the default ``fmin`` or a pre-cue ``baseline`` in that case. Adds an offline regression test on a synthetic tiled file (:gh:`1340` by `Yiheng Li`_).
